-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/7 (19.5.2024), ניכוי שכר לעובדי הוראה בשל השבתת
-- הלימודים במערכת החינוך בשנת הלימודים התשפ"ד
-- No pay for strike time: the owners reduce the pay of teaching employees
-- who took part in the teachers' union's strikes of May 2024 (and any
-- later strike) by the hours they were absent, and the Ministry deducts
-- from its current payments to the owners of the striking institutions.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/7 — ניכוי שכר בשל השבתת הלימודים בשנת הלימודים התשפ"ד`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 The letterhead, date, reference number, addressees (the owners of educational institutions), greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- The rule the circular applies: no pay is paid for strike days
-- (government decisions 647 (כל/168) of 22.4.80 and 646 of 26.5.81); in
-- budgeted bodies, §29 of the Budget Foundations Law requires it.
@ref akn:hc_1/p13
GIVEN `hours on strike` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay owed for strike time` `hours on strike` IS 0

-- The strikes as the circular records them at its writing; its rules hold
-- for any further strike too.
@ref akn:hc_1/p14
`the strikes known at the writing` MEANS
    LIST `strike` (Date 2 5 2024)  8 10 TRUE FALSE,
         `strike` (Date 15 5 2024) 8 10 TRUE FALSE,
         `strike` (Date 19 5 2024) 8 10 TRUE TRUE

@desc A strike the circular names: the day, the hours (24-hour clock) and where it ran.
DECLARE `strike` HAS
    `strike day`         IS A DATE
    `from hour`          IS A NUMBER
    `to hour`            IS A NUMBER
    `in upper-secondary schools` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only in the three cities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the strike ran only in Jerusalem, Tel Aviv-Yafo and Haifa

@ref akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN s IS A `strike`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the strike's hours` s IS
    s's `to hour` MINUS s's `from hour`

GIVEN c IS A `city`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is one of the three cities` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `Jerusalem` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Tel Aviv-Yafo` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Haifa` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `city` IS ONE OF
    `Jerusalem`
    `Tel Aviv-Yafo`
    `Haifa`
    `another city`

-- Whether a strike reached a school: upper-secondary schools, and for the
-- third strike only those in the three cities.
@ref akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN s IS A `strike`, `upper-secondary` IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A `city`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the strike reached` s `upper-secondary` c IF
        (s's `in upper-secondary schools` IMPLIES `upper-secondary`)
    AND (s's `only in the three cities` IMPLIES `is one of the three cities` c)

-- Participation is read off the attendance reports: an employee not
-- present at the strike's time who brought no approval of the absence under
-- the procedures is held to have taken part (in the strike or in the
-- organisational measures).
@ref akn:hc_1/p16
GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the strike`, `known to have taken part` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the employee took part in the strike the union announced, on the owner's knowledge apart from the attendance reports
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `took part in the strike` e `known to have taken part` IF
        `known to have taken part`
    OR (    (NOT e's `present at the time of the strike`)
        AND (NOT e's `brought an approval of the absence`))

@desc A teaching employee at the time of one strike.
DECLARE `employee at the strike` HAS
    `present at the time of the strike`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc by the attendance reports of the workplace
    `brought an approval of the absence`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc brought an approval of the absence under the procedures
    `hours absent from work`                   IS A NUMBER  @desc the hours the employee was absent from work at the strike, teaching-support and individual hours included
    `hourly value`                             IS A NUMBER  @desc the employee's own value of one working hour (ערך השעה), from the employee's salary

-- The reduction: the hours absent times the employee's hourly value;
-- teaching-support hours and individual hours the employee should have
-- done during the strike count among the hours.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the strike`, `known to have taken part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pay reduction` e `known to have taken part` IS
    IF `took part in the strike` e `known to have taken part`
    THEN e's `hours absent from work` TIMES e's `hourly value`
    ELSE 0

-- On the Treasury wage commissioner's instruction, the owner reduces the
-- pay of every teaching employee who took part. The circular sets no month
-- for it, so the duty has no deadline.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p16
GIVEN e IS AN `employee at the strike`, `known to have taken part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the owner reduces the striker's pay` e `known to have taken part` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `reduce the employee's pay` r PROVIDED r EQUALS `the pay reduction` e `known to have taken part`
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the owner must reduce the pay of a teaching employee who took part in the strike by the hours absent"

DECLARE `strike action` IS ONE OF
    `reduce the employee's pay` HAS `reduction` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct from the current MATAM payments` HAS `deducted hours` IS A NUMBER

-- The Ministry, for its part, deducts ("ינכה") from its current MATAM payments to
-- the owner by the budgeted hours of the striking institutions and the
-- strike's times. No deadline is stated.
@ref akn:hc_1/p18
GIVEN `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS A NUMBER @desc the hours budgeted to the owner's institutions that struck, for the strike's times
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the Ministry deducts from the owner's payments` `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `deduct from the current MATAM payments` h PROVIDED h EQUALS `budgeted hours of the striking institutions`
    LEST BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "the Ministry deducts from the current MATAM payments by the budgeted hours of the striking institutions"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off: the signatures and the copies list; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples. The hourly value of 100 is a placeholder: the circular leaves it to each employee's salary.
`absent from 8 to 10 without approval` MEANS
    `employee at the strike` WITH
        `present at the time of the strike`  IS FALSE
        `brought an approval of the absence` IS FALSE
        `hours absent from work`             IS 2
        `hourly value`                       IS 100

`absent with an approved absence` MEANS
    `employee at the strike` WITH
        `present at the time of the strike`  IS FALSE
        `brought an approval of the absence` IS TRUE
        `hours absent from work`             IS 2
        `hourly value`                       IS 100

#ASSERT `the pay reduction` `absent from 8 to 10 without approval` FALSE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the pay reduction` `absent with an approved absence` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD `the strike's hours` s EQUALS 2) `the strikes known at the writing`
#ASSERT `the strike reached` (`strike` (Date 19 5 2024) 8 10 TRUE TRUE) TRUE `Haifa`
#ASSERT NOT `the strike reached` (`strike` (Date 19 5 2024) 8 10 TRUE TRUE) TRUE `another city`
#ASSERT NOT `the strike reached` (`strike` (Date 2 5 2024) 8 10 TRUE FALSE) FALSE `another city`
#ASSERT `pay owed for strike time` 2 EQUALS 0

#TRACE `the owner reduces the striker's pay` `absent from 8 to 10 without approval` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `reduce the employee's pay` 200 AT 1
#TRACE `the Ministry deducts from the owner's payments` 40 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `deduct from the current MATAM payments` 40 AT 1
